--------------------The C# code that corresponds to the assert statement in the comments can be constructed as follows:

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_Ret || Old_arrListCount != -1);
```

This assert statement checks two things: if `New_Ret` is true, it is already true, and if `New_Ret` is false, it checks if `Old_arrListCount` is not -1. The assert statement is used to verify if a certain condition is always true during the execution of the code. If the assert condition fails, it means that there was an error in the logic of the program.
